INSERT OR REPLACE INTO articles
  (slug, desk, article_type, title, dek, brief_html, body_html, respond_html, prospect_html, key_numbers, hero_image, hero_caption, read_time, published_at, tags, toolkit_gated, sources_text)
VALUES (
  '2026/10/15/two-year-yield-94-basis-points-above-policy-rate',
  'economy',
  'article',
  'The Two-Year Yield Sits 94 Basis Points Above the Policy Rate While Two of Three Core Measures Sit Near 2%',
  'Bond markets have repriced the Canadian curve since March while the overnight rate has stayed at 2.25%, and the five-year yield is where fixed mortgage rates take their cue.',
  '<ul>
<li><strong>The curve prices increases,</strong><span> the two-year yield was 3.19% on October 13, 94 basis points above the 2.25% policy rate.</span></li>
<li><strong>Core measures point to target,</strong><span> Continuum Economics expects CPI-Trim at 1.8% and CPI-Median at 1.9% when September CPI is released on October 19.</span></li>
<li><strong>Jobs add a constraint,</strong><span> Canada lost about 68,000 jobs in September and the unemployment rate rose to 6.5%.</span></li>
<li><strong>Mortgages follow the five-year yield,</strong><span> it rose from 3.35% on September 1 to 3.69% on September 23, and the lowest five-year fixed rate was 4.34% on October 14.</span></li>
<li><strong>October 28 brings a new forecast,</strong><span> the Bank of Canada publishes its Monetary Policy Report alongside the decision.</span></li>
</ul>',
  '<p>The Canadian two-year Government of Canada yield closed at 3.19% on October 13, which is 94 basis points above the 2.25% Bank of Canada policy rate. The policy rate has not changed since at least March 2. The five-year yield was 3.55% and the ten-year was 3.87%. A two-year yield that far above the overnight rate is the bond market pricing an eventual path of increases, and it is doing so ahead of the Bank decision on October 28, when the Monetary Policy Report is also due.</p><h2>What the Core Measures Are Expected to Say</h2><p>Statistics Canada reports September consumer prices on Monday, October 19. Continuum Economics expects headline inflation to hold at 3.0% for a third consecutive month, with energy as the upward pressure. Its forecasts for the three Bank of Canada preferred core measures are 1.8% for CPI-Trim, 1.9% for CPI-Median and 2.5% for CPI-Common, each one tenth lower than in August. Two of the three measures would sit below the 2% target and the third would sit half a point above it.</p><p>The labour market adds a second constraint. Canada lost about 68,000 jobs in September and the unemployment rate rose to 6.5% from 6.4%, while average hourly wages grew 2.3% from a year earlier, according to the Financial Post. The Bank therefore faces headline inflation at 3.0% from energy, core measures near target and a weaker labour market. TD Economics and CIBC expect holds, and the odds of an October increase were about 25% after the jobs data, according to LSEG.</p><h2>The Transmission to Fixed Mortgage Rates</h2><p>The Bank of Canada does not set fixed mortgage rates. Five-year fixed rates follow the five-year bond yield plus a lender spread, which Wealth North puts at roughly 1.2 to 2.0 percentage points. That yield rose from 3.35% on September 1 to 3.69% on September 23, a gain of 34 basis points in three weeks, and had eased to 3.55% by October 13. Ratehub listed a lowest five-year fixed rate of 4.34% on October 14, against about 4.24% in September.</p><p>A household renewing a five-year fixed mortgage in the coming months therefore prices the renewal off a bond market in which the five-year yield has risen 79 basis points since March while the policy rate has not moved at all. The five-year yield has moved most, from 2.76% to 3.55%, and the Canadian curve has shifted upward at every maturity.</p><div class="hdq-chart">
<div style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d0d0d0;width:100%;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">
<div style="background:#f5f5f5;border-bottom:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:10px 14px;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
<span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#111;letter-spacing:0.02em;">GOC 2Y, 5Y AND 10Y YIELDS</span>
<span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#111;">3.55%</span>
<span style="font-size:13px;color:#2e7d32;">▲ 79 BP 5Y SINCE MAR 2</span>
<span style="font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-left:auto;">DAILY CLOSE &nbsp;|&nbsp; MAR 2 TO OCT 13, 2026</span>
</div>
<div style="padding:12px 14px 8px;">
